Extended the Task struct with new fields and implemented the import system.

Part A - Task field changes:
- Priority changed from int to string type to use P0-P4 levels where empty
  implies P2. This avoids Go's zero value (0) accidentally meaning P0.
- Added Type (bug/task/feature), CloseReason (free text), and Tags ([]string
  stored comma-separated) fields to the Task struct.
- Added corresponding setter methods (SetType, SetCloseReason, SetTags) that
  keep struct fields and Meta map in sync.
- Updated knownMetaKeys to include type, close-reason, tags so they are
  excluded from the meta JSON field.
- Updated taskMetaOrder for consistent serialization ordering.
- Updated parser.go to parse all new fields from markdown metadata lines,
  with priority now assigned as string directly (no strconv.Atoi).
- Fixed Ready sort to use string comparison with empty defaulting to "P2".
- Removed strconv.Atoi priority conversions from add.go and update.go CLI
  commands; add.go now captures full "P\d" match instead of just the digit.

Part B - Import command:
- Created Importer interface (Name, Import) with registry pattern.
- Created RunImport function that handles deduplication by "<name>-id" meta
  key, loading existing tasks to check for duplicates before calling AddMany.
- Created beadsImporter implementing the interface, running bd list --json
  --all -n 0 and mapping beadIssue fields to Task fields per the specification.
- Status mapping: open→open, in_progress→inprogress, closed→closed,
  blocked/deferred→open with original stored in bead-status meta.
- Priority mapping: beads int 0-4 → P0-P4.
- Added AddMany to meads.go for batch task creation with single lock acquire.
- Added CLI import command registered under "beads" and "bead" aliases.
- Comprehensive tests for beadToTask mapping, RunImport dedup logic, and
  parser round-trips for all new fields.
